    "title": "SAMYANG Original Korean Ramen Multipack 120g × 5",
    "handle": "samyang-ramen-multipack-120g-5pk",
    "body": "<!-- 🚀 Conversion Summary Box -->\n<div style=\"border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; background: #ffffff; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 14px 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<ul style=\"margin: 0; padding-left: 18px;\">\n<li>Korea’s first instant ramen, introduced in 1963</li>\n<li>Classic savory broth with satisfying chewy noodles</li>\n<li>5-pack multipack ideal for families and pantry stocking</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<!-- 🚚 Shipping Information -->\n<div style=\"border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; background: #f9fafb; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4;\">📦 Shipping from Auckland $8.99~ / North Island Zone 1 $12.99~ / North Island Zone 2 $14.99~ / South Island $22.99~ · Free shipping: Auckland $99+ / North Island $150+, $200+ </div>\n<p>삼양 라면 멀티팩 (120g × 5입)</p>\n<h3>Quick Highlight</h3>\n<p>The original SAMYANG Ramen since 1963, known for its savory broth and timeless Korean comfort taste.</p>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>SAMYANG Ramen Multipack represents the origin of Korean instant noodles, first launched in 1963. Featuring a deep, savory soup base and perfectly chewy noodles, it delivers a comforting and familiar flavor that has been enjoyed for generations. This multipack is ideal for family meals, sharing, or keeping a reliable classic ramen on hand for everyday enjoyment.</p>\n<h3>Product Details</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Flavor: Original Korean ramen</li>\n<li>Net Weight: 600g (120g × 5 packs)</li>\n<li>Calories: Approx. 500 kcal per serving</li>\n<li>Type: Instant noodle soup</li>\n<li>Cooking Time: 4–5 minutes</li>\n<li>Packaging: Multipack (5 individual packs)</li>\n<li>Storage: Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight</li>\n<li>Allergens: Contains wheat, soy, milk, egg, pork, beef, and shellfish (clam, squid)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Suggested Uses</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Enjoy as a quick and comforting meal anytime</li>\n<li>Add egg, vegetables, or meat for extra nutrition</li>\n<li>Pair with kimchi for a classic Korean combination</li>\n<li>Perfect for family meals or sharing with friends</li>\n</ul>",
